# Normalize line endings repo-wide: git stores LF (added 2026-07-12 to end perpetual phantom-modified
# flags from pre-existing CRLF blobs) AND every working tree checks out LF, overriding core.autocrlf
# (2026-11-27). Tests that pin file text with `\n` (migration, ci.yml and workflow pins) failed on a
# Windows CRLF checkout while passing in CI; LF everywhere makes the local suite match CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# E11 (2026-11-08): files with a `#!` shebang must keep LF in the working tree too. With
# `* text=auto` + core.autocrlf a Windows checkout rewrites `#!/usr/bin/env node\n` to `...\r\n`,
# and Node's ESM loader then throws "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" on import (this broke
# tests/scripts/check-migrations-applied.test.ts on Windows); bash likewise rejects CRLF scripts.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# Git hook shims are run by sh and must stay LF in every working tree.
scripts/git-hooks/* text eol=lf
